{
  "description": "A family-aware diagnostic adapter for Self-EvolveRec that measures a trained HSTU recommender through the host ModelView interface and produces an interpretation prompt grounded in measured metrics and their definitions.",
  "motivation": "Guide model improvements using reproducible diagnostics while preserving benchmark comparability, preventing unsupported claims about unavailable user traits or metadata, and maintaining one trained model per category.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). Return metrics and metric_definitions. Use the actual view.model and preserve item_emb, log2feats(sequence), predict_score(features, items), user_train, meta_data, and review_data compatibility. Handle B x L left-padded tensors with padding masks and final-nonpadding readout, never count-1. Use only available interaction histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps; treat unavailable attributes as unobserved. Produce full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for five real training users per category. Select changes using host-measured macro validation HR@10 across all four categories. Preserve HSTU, fixed seeds and training limits, and checkpoint/predictor consistency. No measured results are supplied.",
  "pseudocode": "class DiagnosisProbe:\n  initialize(view, device)\n  run_full_diagnosis(train_loader):\n    preserve model training mode\n    put view.model in evaluation mode\n    under no_grad:\n      for (_, sequence, positive, negative) in train_loader:\n        features = view.log2feats(sequence)\n        mask padding and invalid targets\n        accumulate explicitly defined diagnostics using view.predict_score\n      generate unseen-item recommendations for designated training users\n    restore model training mode\n    return {metrics: measured_results, metric_definitions: definitions}\n\ndef diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis):\n  return prompt containing measured metrics, definitions, availability limits,\n         and instructions to distinguish observations from hypotheses",
  "originality": {
    "score": 4,
    "positive": "Combines architecture-aware diagnostics with explicit data-availability and benchmark constraints.",
    "negative": "Primarily an interface and evaluation discipline; it introduces no new learning algorithm or concrete diagnostic metric."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "Could support systematic diagnosis and targeted HSTU improvements under a consistent validation objective.",
    "negative": "Its usefulness depends on selecting informative probes and verifying proposed improvements through controlled validation."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 5,
    "positive": "The required entry points and batch interfaces are clearly specified.",
    "negative": "Correct masking, HSTU feature handling, full-catalog scoring, and preservation of model state require careful integration."
  }
}
